# close-completeness gate — enforcement sentinel (#1290)
#
# This committed marker governs whether the close-completeness gate
# (`deploy.sh --check-close-completeness`, i.e. Check 48's verdict) BLOCKS or merely
# REPORTS on an INCOMPLETE verdict. The probe reads this file directly, so the
# sentinel is load-bearing on its own; a thin CI workflow can additionally consume
# the probe's exit code once wired.
#
# The first non-comment, non-blank line is the mode token. The probe maps every verdict
# through _cc_verdict_exit_code; exit 0 is CLEAN's alone under either token.
#   warn      → a finding reports on advisory exit 2 and a withheld verdict (network leg
#               NOT-EVALUATED, or the gate SKIPped) on exit 3 — reported, not blocking.
#   enforce   → INCOMPLETE and SKIP each exit 1 (red in CI; merge-blocking once the job
#               is a required branch-protection context). NOT-EVALUATED still exits 3 and
#               never blocks: a measurement outage cannot gate under either token.
#
# Stays `warn` during the calibration window, per the warn-mode-initial posture and
# the reflexive-pipeline-loop discipline (the introducing release v2.37 closed under
# the pre-merge runbook; the gate's row-cutover is anchored strictly AFTER that
# merge).
#
# ARMING STATUS (#4176): the row cutover is ARMED. CLOSE_COMPLETENESS_CHECK_CUTOFF now
# ships as a committed default in deploy.sh, so the gate evaluates on every run rather
# than SKIPping — that clause of the graduation path is DISCHARGED and is recorded here
# rather than left as outstanding work. The cutoff was chosen as the oldest value with
# zero standing findings, so the warn log started CLEAN when it was armed. It does not
# read CLEAN now: findings have accrued since — published Release bodies that drifted
# from their notes after release, and rows whose Phase-B Velocity field is missing or
# fails its grammar — so the gate carries a standing INCOMPLETE verdict that the flip
# below must drain first.
#
# REMAINING FLIP-TO-ENFORCE WORK (all four required, none done):
#   1. DRAIN the standing verdict, or allowlist each residual row with a stated reason:
#      re-emit every drifted published body from its note (the release-notes standard's
#      §5.6 re-emit sweep) and backfill or grandfather the Velocity rows. A warn log that
#      still carries known findings can never evidence step 2's zero-false-positive bar.
#   2. Flip the token below to `enforce` after a >=3-day warn-log review with ZERO
#      false positives. Read `"evaluated":false` rows in that log as measurement
#      outages, not findings.
#   3. Add the `close-completeness` job to branch-protection required checks
#      (per core/standards/gate-efficacy-standard.md — a token flip alone does not
#      make the context required).
#   4. Delete the workflow's `paths:` filter (the GRADUATION CLAUSE in
#      .github/workflows/close-completeness.yml): a path-filtered required context
#      leaves every non-matching PR permanently pending.
# At the flip, also decide whether any NOT-EVALUATED cause escalates. Only an input
# failure a pull request can repair is a candidate; a host outage never gates. The
# cause-to-class table on the probe (deploy.sh, cmd_check_close_completeness) is the
# map that decision reads.
#
# (Content-flagged rather than presence-flagged so the file can ship now — the
#  docs reference it — while the gate stays non-blocking; the version-freeness
#  sentinel is presence-flagged, this one is mode-token-flagged.)
warn
